  data: {
    LLM: 'Players place one tile per turn to a legal open end of the shared layout. If blocked, the table profile determines whether to draw from a boneyard or pass. A hand ends when a player empties their hand or when play is blocked, and the table profile determines how the hand is scored.',
    Player: 'Players place one tile per turn to a legal open end of the shared layout. If blocked, the table profile determines whether to draw from a boneyard or pass. A hand ends when a player empties their hand or when play is blocked, and the table profile determines how the hand is scored.',
    objective: 'Play legal tiles by matching open ends and achieve the best score under the match profile when the hand ends.',
    gameplay: 'Players place one tile per turn to a legal open end of the shared layout. If blocked, the table profile determines whether to draw from a boneyard or pass. A hand ends when a player empties their hand or when play is blocked, and the table profile determines how the hand is scored.',
    keyRules: [
      'A played tile must match the value of an exposed open end.',
      'Blocked turns resolve according to the draw-or-pass profile.',
      'Hand-end and scoring vary by table.',
